    "current_example": {
      "math_academy_id": "e-3182",
      "problem": "Carol has to wrap a rope around a circular column whose diameter is $20\\,\\textrm{cm}.$ What length of the rope will wrap the column perfectly?",
      "worked_solution": "The length of the rope needed to wrap around the column is its circumference.\n\nThe formula for the circumference of a circle is $C = \\pi d$, where $d=20\\,\\textrm{cm}$ is the diameter. \n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\nC = \\pi\\cdot 20 = 20\\pi \\,\\textrm{cm}.\n$$",
